#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fix_point

#% text
# `fix_point(f, x)` applies `f` from `x` until the value no longer changes; `fix_point(f, x, n)` at most `n` times.

#% text
# `fix_point(f, x, same_test: g)` stops when `g(previous, next)` is `true`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Numbers that agree count as no change.

#% item
# It is the last value of `fixed_point_list`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fix_point(x => floor(x/2), 100)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
fix_point(cos, 0.7)
#% output
#= 0.7390851332151607

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A test of convergence:

#% cell
fix_point(x => (x + 2/x)/2, 1, same_test: (a, b) => abs(a - b) < 1/10^6)
#% output
#= 886731088897/627013566048

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fixed_point_list`, `nest_while`, `nest`
